## Purpose

Turn Tool Shed's aggregate outcome visibility into a safe, actionable loop-management system. Local
Hybrid state discovers and owns bounded findings; the hosted dashboard remains advisory and hands
the operator a privacy-safe command to paste into the matching local Tool Shed chat.

## Desired Outcome

- Local discovery records stable, deduplicated findings for unhealthy outcome, reconciliation,
  lineage, evidence, propagation, and related document-lifecycle conditions.
- `ts: audit loops` reports current findings and `ts: resolve loop <finding-id>` refreshes local
  authority before selecting or explaining a guarded mitigation.
- A supervised historical mode inventories old conditions without inventing intent or evidence.
- The reporter transports only a bounded, allowlisted projection; the hosted dashboard displays
  each finding with an accessible copy-to-clipboard Tool Shed command.
- Resolution comes from verified local truth and ordinary reporting convergence, never from a
  hosted write, action queue, or remote execution channel.

## System Boundary

| Surface | Authority or role | Boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hybrid SQLite | Authoritative findings, source revisions, lifecycle, recurrence, and local relationships | Findings are diagnostics, not new outcome loops |
| Local Tool Shed routes | Audit, fresh resolution, guarded mitigation, and verification | Existing outcome, campaign, PRM, release, and document engines remain authoritative |
| Reporter | Ordered privacy-bounded projection | Stable public IDs and controlled fields only; no paths, prompts, tokens, diagnostics, or source text |
| Hosted dashboard | Fleet visibility and clipboard handoff | Read-only; cannot enqueue, approve, reconcile, or execute local work |
| Historical review | Deterministic inventory, proposals, reviewed manifests, and evidence | Ambiguous semantic dispositions always remain operator decisions |

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Development outcome | Boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Finding contract and discovery | Stable identity, controlled classes/severity/reasons, observation revisions, recurrence, resolution, limits, and managed-write/safety-pass triggers | No recursive finding-created outcomes |
| Local audit and mitigation | Current/history audits plus fresh finding resolution into existing guarded commands and precise explanations | No stale token replay or authority bypass |
| Historical cleanup | Revision-bound inventories and complete-lineage-cluster manifests with explicit per-item dispositions | No automatic closure or manufactured evidence |
| Reporter and hosted presentation | Source-specific bounded finding payloads, storage, outcome/attention cards, and accessible clipboard behavior | No hosted-to-local intent channel |
| Qualification and release | Migration/rebuild/upgrade parity, browser behavior, and exact-candidate verification across development lanes | Work5 production delivery remains separate |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-FINDING-CONTRACT-AND-DISCOVERY` — freeze and implement the bounded persisted finding model
   and automatic local discovery behavior.
2. `G2-LOCAL-AUDIT-AND-MITIGATION` — implement current/history inspection and fresh local
   mitigation routing through existing guarded engines.
3. `G3-SUPERVISED-HISTORICAL-REVIEW` — implement safe historical inventory, proposal, reviewed
   manifest, application, propagation, verification, and checkpoint behavior.
4. `G4-HOSTED-PROJECTION-AND-CLIPBOARD` — extend the reporter and hosted dashboard while preserving
   the one-way advisory boundary and privacy limits.
5. `G5-DEVELOPMENT-QUALIFICATION-AND-RELEASE-CLOSURE` — qualify migrations and behavior on all
   development lanes, then separately release and recursively reconcile the owning outcome.

## Constraints

- The canonical copied form is `ts: resolve loop <finding-id>`; it contains no path or transient
  authorization material and always triggers a fresh local read.
- The historical success condition is zero unexplained or unclassified loops, not forced
  satisfaction of every old loop.
- Complete-lineage-cluster batching is allowed only when one exact manifest names an explicit
  reviewed disposition for every affected semantic item.
- Resolved findings remain bounded recurrence/history evidence; active and recent projections are
  capped per reporting instance.
- Wrong-workspace, stale, missing, ambiguous, and already-resolved commands fail safely and explain
  the next local action.

